title: c2c new codex can launch with stale global MCP configuration and fail handshake
updated_at: "2026-07-17T11:30:21Z"
---
## Summary

`c2c new codex` launches the managed Codex frontend but depends on the machine-wide c2c MCP block in `~/.codex/config.toml`. If that block is stale, the new managed session starts with a broken c2c MCP server and Codex reports an incomplete MCP startup.

## Observed behaviour

Launching via:

```text
c2c new codex
```

caused Codex to report:

```text
MCP client for `c2c` failed to start: MCP startup failed: handshaking with MCP server failed: connection closed: initialize response
MCP startup incomplete (failed: c2c)
```

The session loaded `[mcp_servers.c2c]` from the global `~/.codex/config.toml` even though the immediate entry point was `c2c new codex`. `codex mcp list` also showed the same globally enabled entry from `/tmp`, confirming this was not project-local configuration.

## Investigation notes

- `c2c install codex` deliberately writes the machine-wide `[mcp_servers.c2c]` block to `~/.codex/config.toml` (`ocaml/cli/c2c_setup.ml`, around line 592 at time of report).
- `c2c new codex` deliberately launches a managed Codex frontend.
- `c2c doctor hooks --compact` reported two stale/missing Codex-managed blocks on the affected machine.
- An empty project `.codex` file was unrelated.
- No configuration changes were made during investigation.

Current dependency chain:

```text
c2c new codex
  -> launches managed Codex
  -> Codex reads ~/.codex/config.toml
  -> globally enabled [mcp_servers.c2c] is stale
  -> c2c MCP handshake fails
```

## Expected behaviour

A managed launch should not silently enter a broken session because previously installed machine-global c2c configuration is stale. `c2c new codex` should either:

1. validate/refresh or safely override the managed c2c MCP definition before launch; or
2. fail before launching with a precise, actionable repair message.

The ownership and lifecycle relationship between `c2c install codex` and `c2c new codex` should be explicit rather than leaving managed launch correctness dependent on stale global state.

## Acceptance criteria

- Add a regression test covering `c2c new codex` with a stale Codex-managed c2c MCP block.
- Managed launch either starts with a current, working c2c MCP definition or stops early with an actionable diagnostic.
- The fix does not make raw `codex` or project-local Codex configuration unexpectedly depend on the current working directory.
- User-facing docs/help explain whether `c2c install codex` is a prerequisite and how stale installed state is repaired.